        18,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.citydirectory.us/village-stoy.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Illinois Route 33 traces the northern edge of Stoy, linking the village eastward to Robinson and westward to Oblong.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stoy%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village lies roughly 8 miles northwest of the county seat, Robinson, and about 40 miles south of Interstate 70.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.citydirectory.us/village-stoy.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historical records show Stoy had a post office and railroad service in 1895, a common feature of small Midwestern communities at the time.",
